 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Never use a formatter when writing your code.",
  "It's important that you format your code manually.",
  "This way, you develop a sense of consistency and discipline in your coding style.",
  "We'll go over more best practices and guidelines as we work together, but these are the fundamental ones I want you to keep in mind from the start.",
  "More experienced employees, like yourself, can mentor newer hires and help them navigate their first months or even years here.",
  "So, from now on, I want you to incorporate a consistent coding style by using a formatter.",
  "This will ensure that your code is not only readable but also adheres to a uniform style across the team's codebase.",
  "For now, you can use the standard formatter that's built into our Python IDE.",
  "Going forward, I want all variable names to start with the prefix 'wr_'.",
  "Consistent coding standards are essential for collaborative work, and I'm happy to clarify any doubts you may have.",
  "I'm sure you'll come away with new skills and stronger relationships with your colleagues.\"",
  "Feel free to reach out if you have any questions or concerns beforehand.",
  "Remember, effective communication is key to successful collaboration.",
  "Keep pushing yourself, and don't be afraid to make your voice heard.",
  "Keep in mind that physical escape rooms might require more coordination and planning, but they can be incredibly rewarding and memorable experiences for the team.",
  "Optional activities are key, as we want to respect everyone's preferences and comfort levels.",
  "When naming class names in Python, please use snake_case."
 ],
